From: conda-forge maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] rapidjson: remove invalid GenericStringRef copy assignment

The vendored cereal 1.2.2 tree ships a copy of rapidjson in which
GenericStringRef defines a copy-assignment operator that assigns to its
own const data members (and never returns a value):

    GenericStringRef& operator=(const GenericStringRef& rhs) { s = rhs.s; length = rhs.length; }

Nothing ever calls it, so older compilers never instantiated the body and
never diagnosed it.  GCC 15 checks uninstantiated template bodies
(-Wtemplate-body) and recent clang eagerly checks the non-dependent
`length = rhs.length;` assignment, so both now fail hard:

    error: assignment of read-only member
      'rapidjson::GenericStringRef<CharType>::length' [-Wtemplate-body]
    error: cannot assign to non-static data member 'length' with
      const-qualified type 'const SizeType'

Upstream rapidjson fixed this by dropping the definition and declaring the
operator private and undefined, next to the equally disallowed non-const
array constructor.  This applies the same change to the vendored copy.

Upstream: https://github.com/Tencent/rapidjson/blob/master/include/rapidjson/document.h
---
--- a/include/cereal/external/rapidjson/document.h
+++ b/include/cereal/external/rapidjson/document.h
@@ -316,8 +316,6 @@
 
     GenericStringRef(const GenericStringRef& rhs) : s(rhs.s), length(rhs.length) {}
 
-    GenericStringRef& operator=(const GenericStringRef& rhs) { s = rhs.s; length = rhs.length; }
-
     //! implicit conversion to plain CharType pointer
     operator const Ch *() const { return s; }
 
@@ -328,6 +326,8 @@
     //! Disallow construction from non-const array
     template<SizeType N>
     GenericStringRef(CharType (&str)[N]) /* = delete */;
+    //! Copy assignment operator not permitted - immutable type
+    GenericStringRef& operator=(const GenericStringRef& rhs) /* = delete */;
 };
 
 //! Mark a character pointer as constant string
